@OrderApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5102
@Gateway_HostAddress = http://localhost:5100
@Keycloak_HostAddress = http://localhost:8180

### Start the AppHost first. The requests go through the gateway and need a token from Keycloak, so run the logins first.

### Login of alice (password: alice) => OK, with the access token for the requests below
# @name alice
POST {{Keycloak_HostAddress}}/realms/cat-demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=cat-demo-cli&username=alice&password=alice

### Login of bob (password: bob) => OK, with the access token for the requests below
# @name bob
POST {{Keycloak_HostAddress}}/realms/cat-demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=cat-demo-cli&username=bob&password=bob

### Login of admin (password: admin) => OK, with the access token for the requests below
# @name admin
POST {{Keycloak_HostAddress}}/realms/cat-demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=cat-demo-cli&username=admin&password=admin

@CatalogApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5101

### Run the requests from top to bottom. Later requests use ids from earlier responses.
### Start Catalog and Orders together, for example with the AppHost. The first request reads the book ids from Catalog,
### because Catalog creates them when it seeds the database and they differ on every machine.
### The token picks the user: alice, bob or admin. Without the AppHost, a plain dotnet run has no login and uses the X-Demo-User header, so these requests need the AppHost.
### Stock and payment come from fakes:
###   a line of more than 50 copies is out of stock,
###   a total above 500 euro is declined.
### Prices come from Catalog when Orders runs under the AppHost. Without the AppHost a fake makes the price from the book id.

### BookSearchRequest (Catalog) => OK (the seeded books, whose ids the orders below use)
# @name books
GET {{CatalogApi_HostAddress}}/catalog/books

### PlaceOrderRequest => Created (alice orders 2 copies of a book)
# @name placed
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "bookId": "{{books.response.body.$[0].id}}", "quantity": 2 },
    { "bookId": "{{books.response.body.$[1].id}}", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### OrderGetListRequest => OK (alice sees her own orders, newest first)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.access_token}}

### OrderGetRequest => OK (the order that was just placed)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.access_token}}

### OrderGetRequest => Not Found, because the order belongs to alice (CAT-GEN-1002)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.$.access_token}}

### OrderGetListRequest => OK (bob has no orders yet)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.$.access_token}}

### OrderGetRequest => OK (an admin sees every order)
GET {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### PlaceOrderRequest => Bad request, out of stock (CAT-ORD-1002). The order is saved with status Cancelled.
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "bookId": "{{books.response.body.$[2].id}}", "quantity": 51 }
  ]
}

### PlaceOrderRequest => Bad request, the payment is declined (CAT-ORD-1003). The order is saved with status Cancelled.
### 100 copies cost far more than the 500 euro limit of the fake, whatever the books cost.
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "bookId": "{{books.response.body.$[3].id}}", "quantity": 50 },
    { "bookId": "{{books.response.body.$[4].id}}", "quantity": 50 }
  ]
}

### PlaceOrderRequest => Bad request, no lines
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": []
}

### PlaceOrderRequest => Bad request, several rules fail (book id and quantity)
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "bookId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "quantity": 0 },
    { "bookId": "{{books.response.body.$[0].id}}", "quantity": 100 }
  ]
}

### CancelOrderRequest => No Content (alice cancels her order)
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.access_token}}

### CancelOrderRequest => Conflict, the order is already cancelled (CAT-ORD-1004)
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.access_token}}

### CancelOrderRequest => Not Found, bob cannot cancel the order of alice
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.$.access_token}}

### CleanUpOrderCountersRequest => No Content
### Development only. It simulates the nightly run of the scheduler.
### Deletes the counters of earlier days and creates the counter of today.
POST {{OrderApi_HostAddress}}/development/scheduler/clean-up-order-counters
